# Little Browser (Android): Peek's "open as tab" keeps the page (docs/ux.md §7, §10). Chromium's
# link-preview sheet opened its address again in a new tab; it now hands its WebContents to the new
# tab, as Custom Tabs' reparenting does, so the page isn't loaded again and keeps its state. A
# sheet given a different full-page address (as some callers do) still opens that address.

